      "customfield_10012" : "0|i0025z:",
      "customfield_10300" : "{}",
      "description" : {
         "content" : [
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "\tAdd somewhere in TODO – that we can have extra ‘thread locking policy’ traits fields in the concrete containers (like bag_linkedlist<>…. So can somehow be assigned to regular bag_linked_list,(not sure how cuz different traits object?).. but doesn’t affect API",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "o\tIdea is maybe we can chose between",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "\tNormal locks",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "\tOptimistic locking",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "\tAssume used from one thread (but in debug builds validates this claim)",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "•\tCall this AssumeExternallySynchonized",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "\tBag<int> b = Bag_LinkedList<Bag_LinkedList_Traits_assume_one_thread<int>> (); ",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "o\tNote someplace – TENTATIVE way to handle (below) optimistic locking stuff – is to do CONCRETE_TRAITS as EXTRA template param for concrete types (like Bag_LinkedList<T, TRAITS (really bagtraits), Bag_LinkedList_IMPL_TRAITS>",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "\tEXPLAIN WHY THIS APPROACH",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "•\tOtherwise – if we embedded impl choices in BASE TRAITS – then assignemtnt to base Bag<T,TRAITS> wouldn’t work right. ",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "•\t",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            }
         ],
         "type" : "doc",
         "version" : 1
      },
